/usr/bin/curl in this image
===========================

What it is
  The statically linked curl 8.11.0 that the upstream MinIO image
  (quay.io/minio/minio:RELEASE.2025-09-07T16-13-09Z) carried: the release
  asset `curl-aarch64` / `curl-amd64` of https://github.com/moparisthebest/static-curl
  tag v8.11.0, unmodified, pinned by the sha256 in that release's sha256sum.txt.
  `curl --version` reports:
    curl 8.11.0 libcurl/8.11.0 OpenSSL/1.1.1t zlib/1.2.12 libssh2/1.9.0 nghttp2/1.43.0
  linked against musl libc.

Why it is here
  Upstream's Dockerfile.release installs it (dockerscripts/download-static-curl.sh),
  so the rebuild does too: a health check written against the upstream image
  as `curl -f http://localhost:9000/minio/health/live` keeps working. Nothing
  Logweir runs calls it (its probes use `mc ready local` or HTTP GETs from the
  kubelet). NOTE: OpenSSL 1.1.1t is past its end of life.

Licences (the texts beside this file)
  curl            curl licence (MIT/X derivative)   curl.COPYING       (curl tag curl-8_11_0)
  OpenSSL 1.1.1t  OpenSSL + SSLeay dual licence     openssl.LICENSE    (tag OpenSSL_1_1_1t)
  zlib 1.2.12     zlib licence                      zlib.LICENSE       (zlib.h of v1.2.12)
  libssh2 1.9.0   BSD-3-Clause                      libssh2.COPYING    (tag libssh2-1.9.0)
  nghttp2 1.43.0  MIT                               nghttp2.COPYING    (tag v1.43.0)
  musl libc       MIT                               musl.COPYRIGHT     (text of musl v1.2.3; the
                                                                        linked musl version is not
                                                                        recorded in the binary)
  static-curl     MIT (the build scripts)           static-curl.LICENSE
